Here are some useful `String` functions. You won't need these until the Spelling Game extension.

# `String.substr_replace_first`

This function replaces the first instance of a substring with a new substring of your
choice in a given input string. It has the following signature:

```val substr_replace_first : ?pos:int -> t -> pattern:t -> with_:t -> t```


# `String.to_list`

This function turns a string into the corresponding list of characters. It has the
following signature:

```val to_list : t -> char list```


# `String.of_list`

This function turns a list of characters into the corresponding string. It has the
following signature:

```val of_list : char list -> t```


# `String.sub`

This function returns the substring corresponding to the starting position within the
base string and the new length that you define. It has the following signature:

```val sub : string -> pos:int -> len:int -> string```

